  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, concat, singleprofile) achieves 0.532 acc, barely above rna_only (0.520), indicating the image modality contributes very little under concat fusion. scvi_n200 clearly outperforms scgpt (~10 pt gap). The key uncertainty is whether the near-zero image contribution is due to the fusion mechanism (concat vs. weighted) or to the image representation itself. Question tested: config_051 is identical to config_002 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the effect of fusion strategy on how much the image modality can contribute. Why best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable comparison from the current best configuration, directly tests whether a better fusion mechanism can unlock image value, and the answer (weighted helps or not) will determine whether subsequent budget should go toward multiprofile/aggregation (if fusion was the bottleneck) or toward a different image encoder (if the image features are inherently weak). This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

